Independently authored. It recreates the method and look of NODE's Measured Light
holograms without including any NODE code, fonts, shaders or assets.

Third-party software: none is bundled. The toolkit uses the Python standard library only;
the viewer is plain WebGL2 and uses system fonts. Optional programs it can call when they
are already installed: a Chromium-family browser (review captures) and ffmpeg (video). Each
keeps its own licence and is never downloaded or installed by this toolkit.

Example artwork (hologram_studio/examples/v2/assets) is synthetic, generated by png.py, and
labelled as generated decoration. No authentic artwork, private data, credentials or model
weights are included.

History: extracted from the hologram-skill branch of the Tessera project, where the same
author wrote it (first under Apache-2.0); relicensed under MIT by its author.
